Source: luma-desktop
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Projeto Luma <luma-dev@example.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), librsvg2-bin, python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: luma-theme
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, plasma-workspace (>= 4:6.3), kwin-common (>= 4:6.3), breeze, breeze-cursor-theme, papirus-icon-theme, fonts-inter,
 plasma-nm, plasma-pa, qml6-module-org-kde-bluezqt, qml6-module-org-kde-kcmutils
Recommends: luma-ajustes
Description: Luma desktop theme for KDE Plasma
 Global themes (light and dark), color schemes, panel layout with a top
 bar and a floating dock, and the Luma Aurora wallpaper. Reuses Breeze for
 widgets, window decorations and icons.

Package: luma-session
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, luma-theme (= ${source:Version}), plasma-workspace (>= 4:6.3), fonts-inter
Recommends: plasma-discover, plasma-discover-backend-flatpak, xdg-desktop-portal-kde
Description: Luma default session settings for KDE Plasma
 Makes the Luma global theme, panel layout and lock screen the defaults for
 new users, overriding the Debian defaults through /etc/xdg. Settings users
 have already chosen are kept.

Package: luma-firewall
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ufw
Recommends: plasma-firewall
Description: Luma default firewall policy
 Enables ufw once with incoming connections denied and outgoing allowed,
 unless the administrator has already enabled it. Later changes made by the
 administrator are kept.

Package: luma-ajustes
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-pyside6.qtquick, python3-pyside6.qtqml,
 qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami, luma-theme (= ${source:Version}), kde-cli-tools, plasma-workspace
Description: Luma settings app (appearance)
 Light or dark appearance, accent color, transparency, animations and text
 size, using the existing Plasma tools. Other sections open the matching
 System Settings modules.

Package: luma-live
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, live-config, calamares
Description: Luma live session settings
 live-config component that keeps the live session from locking the screen
 or suspending while the installer runs, and an installer step that completes
 the UEFI removable-media boot path of the installed system. Only meant for
 the live image; the installer removes this package from the installed system.

Package: luma-windows
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, wine, wine64, kdialog
Recommends: wine32
Description: Luma best-effort launcher for Windows programs
 Opens .exe and .msi files with Debian's Wine on double click, after a
 first-use warning. Nothing is promised about the program working, and Wine
 is not a security boundary: the program runs as the user with access to the
 same files. 32-bit programs need wine32 from the i386 architecture.
